2c:["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]
2d:["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Magnific is a creative upscaler: you feed it an image and it enlarges it while inventing plausible new detail, texture and lighting, with sliders to control how much it reimagines versus preserves the original. That hallucination is its strength and its risk, which is why control over how much it changes the image matters. In Melius, upscaling and enhancement are connected nodes in a larger pipeline rather than a standalone round trip."}]
2e:["$","details","4",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Is Magnific's upscaler better than Melius?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Magnific's creative upscaler is genuinely strong at inventing plausible detail, and for pure maximum-detail upscaling it is a specialist worth using. Melius optimizes for the whole creative pipeline instead of one step, so the question is less which upscaler wins and more whether you want a standalone enhancer or a workspace where enhancement is one connected node."}]]}]
2f:["$","details","5",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Does Melius have a canvas?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. Melius is built canvas-first: a node-based canvas where prompts, images, video and audio are connected nodes, with Mel to plan and wire the work and real-time multiplayer for teams."}]]}]
31:["$","$L30","post-connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp",{"post":{"_key":"post-connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","slug":"connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","category":"modus-news","title":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas with MCP","isoDate":"2026-07-20","date":"July 20, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas over MCP and skip the context drift you get from copy-pasting into a chatbot. The Model Context Protocol exposes the Melius canvas as live, structured data an agent can read and act on. Here is how to connect Claude to Melius, what the tools actually are, and why the loop self-corrects.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the Model Context Protocol (MCP)?","answer":"MCP is an open standard that lets an AI agent connect to a server and call the tools and resources that server exposes. It started with IDEs and terminals, and the same pattern lets an agent read and act on a live creative canvas instead of a screenshot."},{"question":"What is Claude MCP?","answer":"Claude MCP just means using the Model Context Protocol with Claude as the host: Claude connects to an MCP server and calls the tools it exposes. Point it at the Melius connector and Claude can read and act on your live canvas directly, rather than working from a pasted description. The protocol is host-agnostic, so any MCP-compatible model works the same way."},{"question":"How do I connect Claude to Melius?","answer":"The recommended path is the hosted connector. Add a custom MCP connector in your host and point it at https://mcp.melius.com/mcp, then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. Melius mints a durable, revocable connector key for that team, so there is nothing to paste and nothing to refresh."},{"question":"Does the agent generate the images and video itself?","answer":"No. The host model (for example Claude) is the agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do. The images, video, and audio are produced by the generation models available on the platform, selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate."},{"question":"Can I use a model other than Claude?","answer":"Yes. Because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any MCP-compatible host. Melius is model-agnostic at the host level."},{"question":"What stops the agent from acting on nodes that no longer exist?","answer":"The platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas, so if it references something that is no longer there, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"a-standard-bridge-for-creative-work","title":"The MCP bridge"},{"_key":"connecting-claude-to-melius","title":"Connecting Claude"},{"_key":"a-self-correcting-loop","title":"Self-correcting loop"},{"_key":"bring-your-own-model","title":"Bring your own model"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b717","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b714","text":"When you work with a large language model in a creative environment, the most common point of failure isn't the model's reasoning, it's the data it can see. Many workflows still rely on a copy-paste style, where a person describes a canvas, a prompt, or a generated result to a chatbot by hand. That inevitably leads to ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b715","text":"context drift","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b716","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b721","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b718","text":"Context drift is when an agent's understanding of a project diverges from the actual state of the work over time. Standard LLM chats are stateless and disconnected from the tool's live state, so the agent loses track of which nodes exist, how they're wired, and which generation produced which output. It might ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b719","text":"remember","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b720","text":" a video node from three prompts ago with no way of knowing it was since deleted, re-run with a different model, or rewired to a new source image. Without a protocol-level bridge, the model stays blind and you become the manual data translator.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b723","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b722","text":"A standard bridge for creative work","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-standard-bridge-for-creative-work"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b732","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b725","href":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b724","text":"Can a standard protocol close the gap between creative software and external AI models? The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b726","text":"Model Context Protocol (MCP)","marks":["b725"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b727","text":" helps by defining an open interface that lets an agent connect to a server and call its exposed ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b728","text":"tools","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b729","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b730","text":"resources","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b731","text":". The developer community first adopted MCP to connect LLMs to IDEs and terminals, but the same pattern applies to creative software: expose the workspace as structured, queryable data instead of a flat screenshot.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b740","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b733","text":"Melius does exactly this. Its canvas is organized as Team â†’ Projects â†’ Canvas â†’ Nodes + Edges â†’ Runs. A canvas is a 2D workspace; ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b734","text":"nodes","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b735","text":" are creative units (text prompts, images, videos, audio, files); ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b736","text":"edges","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b737","text":" wire nodes together to pass data between them; and a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b738","text":"run","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b739","text":" executes AI generation on a node, taking its prompt, model config, and upstream inputs and producing an output. Over MCP, an agent reads that live node-and-edge graph and acts on it directly, rather than guessing from a description.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b742","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b741","text":"Connecting Claude to Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"connecting-claude-to-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b749","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b746","href":"https://docs.melius.com/mcp/overview","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b743","text":"Connecting takes a couple of minutes. The quickest path is the hosted connector: add a custom MCP connector in your host, point it at ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b744","text":"https://mcp.melius.com/mcp","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b745","text":", then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. For the full walkthrough, including the local server for development and how credentials work, see the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b747","text":"Melius MCP docs","marks":["b746"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b748","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b751","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b750","text":"What the agent can actually do","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b753","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b752","text":"Once connected, the host gets a focused set of capabilities that mirror how the canvas works, rather than one opaque API. At a high level, an agent can:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b756","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b754","text":"Read the live canvas","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b755","text":": what's on it, how the pieces are wired together, and each one's current output, all from the same live state your browser sees","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b759","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b757","text":"Understand what's possible","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b758","text":": which generation models are available and what each one needs, so it works from real capabilities instead of guessing","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b762","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b760","text":"Compose the work","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b761","text":": add, arrange, and wire together the pieces of a creative pipeline","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b765","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b763","text":"Run and follow through","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b764","text":": kick off generations and act on the results as they come back","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b772","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b769","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b766","text":"So a prompt like ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b767","text":"generate a product shot, then animate it into a 5-second clip","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b768","text":" becomes a short pipeline the agent assembles and runs on the real canvas, not a visual approximation. It is the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b770","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b769"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b771","text":" driven from your own agent. The exact shape of that surface is where a lot of the craft lives, so we'll leave the finer mechanics to the platform.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b774","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b773","text":"A self-correcting loop","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-self-correcting-loop"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b776","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b775","text":"One genuinely useful property falls out of exposing the canvas as structured data: the platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas. If it references something that no longer exists, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state. A common failure mode, an agent confidently referencing something that isn't there, becomes a caught error and a re-scan, so the agent corrects itself instead of silently producing broken or failed work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b778","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b777","text":"Bring your own model","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"bring-your-own-model"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b782","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b779","text":"Melius is model-agnostic at the host level: because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any compatible host. Keep the two ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b780","text":"models","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b781","text":" in play distinct. The host model is the reasoning agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do; the generation models, the ones that actually produce images, video, and audio, are the ones available on the platform and selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b787","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b784","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b783","text":"By connecting the Melius MCP server, you aren't bolting on a black-box AI button, you're giving an external agent live, structured access to your canvas, so it has the context it needs to be genuinely useful. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b785","text":"Start creating with Melius","marks":["b784"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b786","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b789","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b788","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b790","items":"$31:props:post:faq"}]}}]
32:["$","$L30","post-one-subscription-every-model",{"post":{"_key":"post-one-subscription-every-model","slug":"one-subscription-every-model","category":"modus-news","title":"One subscription, every model: an all-in-one AI aggregator guide","isoDate":"2026-07-17","date":"July 17, 2026","readTime":"7 Min Read","excerpt":"An AI aggregator puts every model, text, image, video and audio, under one subscription instead of a fragmented stack that clears $100 a month. Here is why aggregators are winning, what a true all-in-one creative AI platform must deliver, and a three-step plan to consolidate your workflow onto a single canvas.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/one-subscription-every-model/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"Can a single subscription truly replace specialized AI tools without losing quality?","answer":"Yes, provided the platform maintains direct API parity with flagship models like Kling and ElevenLabs. Melius achieves this by acting as a unified creative canvas where you can generate a cinematic shot in Kling, overlay a voiceover from ElevenLabs, and refine the prompt with a frontier text model, all within the same interface. This consolidation doesn't just lower monthly costs; it removes the cognitive load of switching contexts, so you focus on the narrative rather than the tech stack."},{"question":"What is subscription bloat, or the AI tax?","answer":"Subscription bloat is what happens when a creative stack is assembled one $20 tool at a time. Text generation, voiceover, image generation, and video generation each arrive as a separate subscription, and a typical stack easily clears $100 a month. The hidden cost isn't only the dollar amount, it's the friction of four interfaces, four credit systems, and four usage caps that can't share quota."},{"question":"What is an AI aggregator?","answer":"An AI aggregator is a platform that consolidates specialized generative engines, for image, video, and audio, into a single workflow and one billing umbrella. Instead of subscribing to each provider directly, you access frontier models like Kling and Seedance for video, GPT Image 2 and Nano Banana Pro for images, and ElevenLabs and Seed Audio for audio through one interface, with one credit pool and one place your assets live. The best aggregators go further, adding a shared context and an agent that orchestrates those models for you rather than just listing them."},{"question":"What is the best AI aggregator?","answer":"The best AI aggregator is the one that does more than list models behind one login. Look for three things: real API parity with the flagship models (so quality isn't sacrificed for convenience), one shared credit pool so you aren't rationing across silos, and an orchestration layer, a canvas plus an agent, that wires the models together and prompts each one correctly. Melius is built around exactly that: every major model on a node-based canvas, one credit pool, and Mel, an agent that plans and routes the work."},{"question":"Why does an aggregator get better results than using the models directly?","answer":"Because access to the models is only half the problem, the other half is orchestration. Melius is built on a node-based creative canvas where every prompt, image, video, and audio track is a connected node, so the output of one model can flow into the next and every generation shares the same brief and brand context. On top of that sits Mel, an agent that can see the whole graph, choose the right model for each step, wire the workflow together, and write the specific prompt each model responds to. A flat list of APIs can't do that, which is why context across models and agentic orchestration are what actually make the results land."},{"question":"What is model agnosticism, and why does it matter?","answer":"Model agnosticism means your workflow isn't locked to a single provider. When a new version of a model drops, an aggregator can add it to the existing dashboard, so you select it from a dropdown instead of buying another subscription or rebuilding your process. It lets you take a best-of-breed approach, testing one model for lighting and another for character consistency, for the price of one."},{"question":"How much can I save by consolidating AI subscriptions?","answer":"A fragmented stack of scripting, voiceover, imagery, and animation tools typically runs $82 to $102 per month. Moving that work onto a single aggregator can lower monthly costs by up to 60%, and it recovers the time otherwise lost to managing billing cycles and switching tabs."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"the-hidden-cost-of-the-fragmented-ai-stack","title":"The hidden cost"},{"_key":"defining-the-all-in-one-creative-standard","title":"The standard"},{"_key":"melius-consolidating-your-creative-workflow","title":"Consolidating"},{"_key":"why-the-canvas-and-the-agent-are-the-real-unlock","title":"Canvas & agent"},{"_key":"performance-vs-price-why-aggregators-are-winning","title":"Why aggregators win"},{"_key":"how-to-migrate-your-creative-projects-to-a-unified-platform","title":"How to migrate"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b527","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b526","text":"The math for a modern creative professional is increasingly broken. If you want the best text generation, you pay OpenAI $20. For high-end voiceovers, ElevenLabs takes another $22. If you need cinematic video generation, a Kling or Luma subscription adds roughly $30. Throw in a specialized image generator like Midjourney or a Flux-based tool for another $10 to $30, and your monthly AI tax easily clears $100.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b531","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b528","text":"This is ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b529","text":"subscription bloat","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b530","text":". We are living through the fragmented creative stack era, where creators spend as much time managing billing cycles and switching tabs as they do actually creating. The solution isn't to stop using these models, it's to change how you access them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b533","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b532","text":"The hidden cost of the fragmented AI stack","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-hidden-cost-of-the-fragmented-ai-stack"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b535","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b534","text":"The financial burden of AI is often underestimated because it creeps in $20 at a time. But the true cost isn't just the dollar amount, it's the friction. Consider a typical video production workflow:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b536","rows":[{"_key":"b537","cells":[{"_key":"b538","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b540","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b539","text":"Stage","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b541","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b543","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b542","text":"Typical tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b544","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b546","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b545","text":"Monthly cost","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b547","cells":[{"_key":"b548","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b550","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b549","text":"Scripting","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b551","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b553","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b552","text":"ChatGPT","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b554","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b556","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b555","text":"$$20","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b557","cells":[{"_key":"b558","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b560","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b559","text":"Voiceover","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b561","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b563","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b562","text":"ElevenLabs (Creator tier)","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b564","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b566","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b565","text":"$$22","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b567","cells":[{"_key":"b568","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b570","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b569","text":"Visuals","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b571","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b573","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b572","text":"Midjourney or Flux","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b574","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b576","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b575","text":"$$10â€“$30","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b577","cells":[{"_key":"b578","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b580","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b579","text":"Animation","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b581","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b583","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b582","text":"Kling AI or Luma Dream Machine","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b584","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b586","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b585","text":"$$30","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b587","cells":[{"_key":"b588","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b590","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b589","text":"Total","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b591","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b593","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b592","text":"Four interfaces, four silos","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b594","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b596","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b595","text":"$$82â€“$102","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b598","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b597","text":"This fragmented stack forces you to navigate four different interfaces, four different credit systems, and four different usage caps. If you hit a limit on Kling, you can't borrow credits from your unused ElevenLabs quota. You're locked into silos. This inefficiency is the primary driver behind the rise of AI aggregators, platforms that consolidate these specialized engines into a single, cohesive workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b600","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b599","text":"Defining the all-in-one creative standard","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"defining-the-all-in-one-creative-standard"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b604","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b601","text":"Not every platform that claims to be all-in-one actually delivers. Many are simply LLM wrappers, interfaces that connect to a chat model and maybe one basic image generator. To be a true creative powerhouse, a platform must master the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b602","text":"Triple Threat","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b603","text":" of modalities:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b607","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b605","text":"Image generation. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b606","text":"A spread of state-of-the-art models like GPT Image 2, Nano Banana Pro, and Seedream, which handle text-in-image, style control, and anatomical accuracy far better than older models. No single one wins every brief, so you want the choice.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b610","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b608","text":"Video generation. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b609","text":"Access to frontier models like Kling and Seedance, capable of consistent physics and high-resolution motion.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b613","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b611","text":"Audio generation. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b612","text":"High-fidelity voice synthesis and music from ElevenLabs, plus reference-driven voices from ByteDance's Seed Audio.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b615","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b614","text":"When evaluating a unified platform, use this checklist to make sure you aren't sacrificing quality for convenience:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b618","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b616","text":"API parity. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b617","text":"Does the platform offer the same settings (guidance scale, seed control, aspect ratios) as the native tools?","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b621","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b619","text":"Model latency. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b620","text":"Is there a significant delay between clicking generate and the model responding?","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b624","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b622","text":"Modal diversity. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b623","text":"Does it cover the full Triple Threat, or is it heavily weighted toward just text?","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b626","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b625","text":"Melius: consolidating your creative workflow","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"melius-consolidating-your-creative-workflow"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b640","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b627","text":"Melius is built specifically to bridge the gap between high-end generative power and cost-efficiency. By integrating frontier models like ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b628","text":"Kling","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b629","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b630","text":"Seedance","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b631","text":" for video, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b632","text":"GPT Image 2","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b633","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b634","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b635","text":" for imagery, and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b636","text":"ElevenLabs","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b637","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b638","text":"Seed Audio","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b639","text":" for audio under one billing umbrella, it eliminates the need for a dozen separate logins.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b642","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b641","text":"Can a single subscription truly replace specialized AI tools without losing quality?","marks":["strong"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b644","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b643","text":"Yes, provided the platform maintains direct API parity with flagship models like Kling and ElevenLabs. Melius achieves this by acting as a unified creative canvas where you can generate a cinematic shot in Kling, overlay a voiceover from ElevenLabs, and refine the prompt with a frontier text model, all within the same interface. This consolidation doesn't just lower monthly costs by up to 60%, it removes the cognitive load of switching contexts, letting you focus on the narrative rather than the tech stack.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b648","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b645","text":"The advantage here isn't just the unified billing, it's the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b646","text":"unified interface","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b647","text":". In a fragmented stack, your assets are scattered across four different gallery pages. In Melius, your video, audio, and images live in a single project ecosystem, making it significantly easier to iterate on a concept without losing your momentum.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b650","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b649","text":"Why the canvas and the agent are the real unlock","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-the-canvas-and-the-agent-are-the-real-unlock"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b656","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b651","text":"Access to every model is table stakes. A dropdown of frontier engines is only as good as your ability to point the right one at the right job and prompt it well, and that is exactly where a bare LLM wrapper falls down. Melius is built on two things a flat list of models doesn't have: a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b652","text":"node-based creative canvas","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b653","text":" and an ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b654","text":"agentic harness","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b655","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b666","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b660","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b663","href":"/blog/seedance-2-5-anticipation","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b657","text":"On the canvas, every prompt, image, video clip, and audio track is a node, and the edges between them carry data from one step to the next. An image node feeds a video node, a script node feeds a voiceover, a still becomes the key frame for a shot. The structure of your project is visible and connected, not buried in a dozen separate chat histories. That shared graph is what gives the platform ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b658","text":"context across models","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b659","text":": the output of a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b661","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["b660"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b662","text":" image can flow directly into a Kling or ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b664","text":"Seedance","marks":["b663"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b665","text":" video, and the same brief and brand context inform every generation on the board.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b670","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b667","text":"Sitting on top of that canvas is Mel, the built-in creative-director agent. Because Mel can see the whole graph, it does the part most people get wrong on their own: it ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b668","text":"orchestrates","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b669","text":" the work. It decides which model fits each step, wires the nodes together in the right order, and translates your intent into the specific prompt each model actually responds to. Kling wants motion described a certain way; an image model wants composition and lens; ElevenLabs wants direction on tone and pacing. Mel handles that per-model prompt craft so you don't have to learn the quirks of ten different tools.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b677","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b674","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b671","text":"This is why the platform gets more ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b672","text":"right","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b673","text":" than a raw list of APIs ever could. The models are the engines, but the canvas gives them shared context and the agent knows how to drive them. A single creative director can hand Mel a brief and get back a coherent, multi-model workflow, generated, connected, and on-brand, the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b675","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b674"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b676","text":" in one place, instead of manually copying assets between four tabs and re-explaining the concept to each one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b679","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b678","text":"Performance vs. price: why aggregators are winning","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"performance-vs-price-why-aggregators-are-winning"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b681","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b680","text":"The legacy model of AI subscriptions asks you to bet on a single horse. If you subscribe to one specific video generator, you're stuck with their version of reality for the month. If a better model drops two weeks later, you're either stuck or paying for a second subscription.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b685","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b682","text":"The aggregator model offers ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b683","text":"model agnosticism","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b684","text":". This is the ultimate future-proofing for a creator. When a new version of Flux or a new competitor to Kling is released, an aggregator like Melius can integrate it into the existing dashboard. You don't have to change your workflow or update your billing, you just select the new model from a dropdown.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b687","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b686","text":"This flexibility allows for a best-of-breed approach. You might find that for a specific project, one model handles lighting better while another handles character consistency. On an aggregator platform, you can test both for the price of one, rather than being locked into the limitations of a single provider.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b689","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b688","text":"How to migrate your creative projects to a unified platform","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"how-to-migrate-your-creative-projects-to-a-unified-platform"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b691","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b690","text":"Transitioning from a fragmented stack to a unified platform like Melius doesn't have to happen overnight. Here is a practical three-step plan to reclaim your workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b694","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b692","text":"The subscription audit. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b693","text":"List every AI tool you currently pay for. Identify the usage gap, models you pay $20 a month for but only use three or four times. These are the first candidates for consolidation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b697","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b695","text":"The output benchmark. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b696","text":"Before canceling your standalone subscriptions, run your most common prompts through Melius. Compare the Kling video output or the ElevenLabs voice clarity against the native apps. With proper API integration, you'll find the results are identical.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b700","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b698","text":"Centralize your assets. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b699","text":"Start a new project within Melius and generate all assets (image, video, and audio) for that specific campaign in the unified canvas. Once you experience the lack of tab-switching, the friction of the old fragmented way becomes much more apparent.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b705","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b702","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b701","text":"The era of paying for five different $20 subscriptions is ending. By moving to a unified platform, you aren't just saving money, you're buying back the time and mental energy required to actually be a creator. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b703","text":"Start creating with Melius","marks":["b702"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b704","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b707","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b706","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b708","items":"$32:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b713","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b710","href":"/blog/ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b709","text":"For a film-specific comparison of shot control, continuity and editing, read ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b711","text":"AI video generators for filmmakers, compared","marks":["b710"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b712","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}]
